[=== ITEMS ===]
The doorbell is scenery.
The description of the doorbell is "A small brass button set into a plate beside the door, the enamel worn at the center from years of use. There is a name engraved on it: 'Wimmer'"

Understand "bell" as the doorbell.

The door across the hall is a door.
The door across the hall is locked.
The door across the hall is scenery.
The description of the door across the hall is "A heavy door, its upper half frosted glass. It looks the same as your apartment door."

Instead of ringing the doorbell:
	say "A harsh electric buzz sounds somewhere inside the apartment. Then nothing."

